# `delete` takes a key out of a map, and stops at run time on a list. A list
# it is handed is refused at check when the list is certain: a name bound to
# a list literal in the same body, or a call whose every arm answers a list.
# A list literal written in place was refused already.
fn filled n
  [n n n]

fn drop_middle n
  xs = [1 2 n]
  delete xs 2

fn drop_made n
  delete (filled n) 2

pub play = print "{drop_middle 9} {drop_made 4}"
